      "role": "user",
      "content": "Task Guide:\n\n\nTask: Aluminum NVT Equilibration for melting\nDescription: Given paths to LAMMPs compatible Aluminum structure file and Embedded Atom Method potential file appropriate for MD simulations, equilibrate the system under NVT conditions with the given simulation parameters. The simulation should replicate the unit cell 5 times in x, y and z direction. Return the absolute path of the equilibrated structure file and the final density in g/cm^3.\n\nRequired submission format:\n{\"density\": \"<numerical_value without units>\", \"path to relaxed structure\": \"<absolute_path>\"} e.g. {\"density\": \"56.00\", \"path to relaxed structure\": \"/structures/structure.dat\"}\n\n\nAvailable input data:\nAll the potentials, can be found at /potentials/. Note that in case of reaxff potentials, pair style 'reax/c' has been renamed to 'reaxff' and always use NULL for the control file (cfile), for example, this syntax is correct : pair_style reaxff NULL.\n\n- Input from aluminum_structure_retrieval_subtask_melting: /results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_structure_retrieval_subtask_melting_trial_1/aluminum_structure.data\n- Input from aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting: /results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting_trial_1/Al99.eam.alloy\n- units: metal\n- pbc: true\n- timestep: 1 femtosecond\n- nvt steps: 10000\n- nvt temperature: 300\n- nvt thermostat: Nose-Hoover\n- atom_style: atomic\n\nIMPORTANT: You have access to filesystem tools. All files will be saved in your isolated workspace.\n Save all the files in /results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_nvt_subtask_melting_trial_1 when using tools use this path.\n\n\nThis task uses output from tasks: aluminum_structure_retrieval_subtask_melting (available), aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting (available)\n\nYou must think what to do next. You can use some of the tools